{"dossier":"D05","entry_points":[{"sids":["include/linux/mmzone.h::local_memory_node","include/linux/mmzone.h::zone_idx","include/linux/mmzone.h::zone_is_zone_device.alt_1","include/linux/mmzone.h::zone_is_zone_device.alt_2","include/linux/mmzone.h::managed_zone","include/linux/mmzone.h::populated_zone"],"text":"Local mapping is identity. Index offsets from node base; device test compares index in one build and fails in the other; managed and populated test nonzero counts."},{"sids":["include/linux/mmzone.h::pfn_to_section_nr","include/linux/mmzone.h::section_nr_to_pfn","include/linux/mmzone.h::SECTION_ALIGN_UP","include/linux/mmzone.h::SECTION_ALIGN_DOWN","include/linux/mmzone.h::__nr_to_section","include/linux/mmzone.h::__section_mem_map_addr","include/linux/mmzone.h::__pfn_to_section","include/linux/mmzone.h::subsection_map_index"],"text":"Numbers convert by shifting with align helpers. Index maps via root division with null on missing roots; address masks flag bits; subsection derives from offset."},{"sids":["include/linux/page_frag_cache.h::page_frag_alloc_align","include/linux/page_frag_cache.h::page_frag_alloc","include/linux/page_reporting.h::page_reporting_dev_info"],"text":"Allocation takes cache, size and flags with optional power-of-two alignment or default shorthand. Reporting exposes callback plus background work."}],"exports":[{"sids":["include/linux/nodemask.h::node_set","include/linux/nodemask.h::node_isset","include/linux/nodemask.h::__nodes_empty"],"text":"Masks support single-bit set/clear, whole fill, and queries for membership, set relations, equality, overlap, subset, emptiness, fullness and count. Only test-and-set reports prior state atomically."},{"sids":["include/linux/nodemask.h::node_state.alt_1","include/linux/nodemask.h::node_state.alt_2","include/linux/nodemask.h::node_set_state.alt_2","include/linux/nodemask.h::node_clear_state.alt_2","include/linux/nodemask.h::num_node_state.alt_2"],"text":"Per-state accessors test, set, clear and count nodes in a global table. Single-node builds reduce test to identity, make updates no-ops, and fix count at one."},{"sids":["include/linux/pageblock-flags.h::get_pageblock_skip.alt_1","include/linux/pageblock-flags.h::clear_pageblock_skip.alt_1","include/linux/pageblock-flags.h::set_pageblock_skip.alt_1","include/linux/pageblock-flags.h::get_pageblock_skip.alt_2","include/linux/pageblock-flags.h::clear_pageblock_skip.alt_2","include/linux/pageblock-flags.h::set_pageblock_skip.alt_2"],"text":"Skip flag is queried, cleared and set in one build; the other always reports clear and ignores updates."}],"extracts":["5e5409e45a1a9c3a42392b87e55c0dadd3c14c33855c88ac95134e257deb9a97","7607a733ffbb8f20b9800b9d1568448006c8a59898c2b425847382f205db095e","e1c9c509f66954fa083c89af8301d01014a2695c98091806ce831da6b775ef21"],"gpl_spec":"PASS","hazards":[{"sids":["include/linux/mmzone.h::__nr_to_section","include/linux/mmzone.h::pfn_valid","include/linux/mmzone.h::first_valid_pfn","include/linux/mmzone.h::pfn_section_valid.alt_1","include/linux/mmzone.h::pfn_section_first_valid.alt_1","include/linux/nodemask.h::node_set","include/linux/nodemask.h::node_isset","include/linux/nodemask.h::next_node_in","include/linux/nodemask.h::NODE_MASK_NONE","include/linux/page_ext.h::page_ext_iter_next"],"text":"Handle null roots/usage as absence, early sections as valid, and hold scheduler protection across checks. Range-check singleton shifts; parsing can fail; lookup at boundaries. Bit, bitmap and RCU helpers are external."},{"sids":["include/linux/page_ref.h::page_ref_unfreeze","include/linux/page_ref.h::folio_ref_unfreeze","include/linux/page_frag_cache.h::page_frag_alloc_align"],"text":"Unfreeze requires zero current and nonzero replacement. Non-power-of-two alignment warns once yet delegates."}],"invariants":[{"sids":["include/linux/mmzone.h::pglist_data","include/linux/mmzone.h::node_present_pages","include/linux/mmzone.h::node_spanned_pages","include/linux/mmzone.h::node_start_pfn","include/linux/mmzone.h::node_end_pfn","include/linux/mmzone.h::pgdat_end_pfn"],"text":"Accessors resolve via node table. Present counts usable pages, spanned includes holes; end equals start plus spanned."},{"sids":["include/linux/nodemask.h::first_online_node.alt_2","include/linux/nodemask.h::node_state.alt_2","include/linux/nodemask.h::node_random","include/linux/page_counter.h::page_counter_reset_watermark","include/linux/page_ext.h::page_ext_init_flatmem_late.alt_1","include/linux/page_ext.h::page_ext_init.alt_1","include/linux/page_ext.h::page_ext_iter_next"],"text":"Single-node fixes first online/memory to zero with immediate end and zero random choice. Watermark writes local before shared. Fast advance needs lookup at section boundaries in one build."},{"sids":["include/linux/page_ref.h::folio_ref_count","include/linux/page_ref.h::page_count","include/linux/page_ref.h::folio_set_count","include/linux/page_frag_cache.h::PAGE_FRAG_CACHE_PFMEMALLOC_BIT","include/linux/page_frag_cache.h::encoded_page_decode_pfmemalloc","include/linux/page_frag_cache.h::page_frag_cache_is_pfmemalloc"],"text":"Page and folio counts share one value in the first page. Cache word keeps order in low bits and reserve origin in a higher bit, decoded independently."},{"sids":["include/linux/page_owner.h::reset_page_owner.alt_1","include/linux/page_table_check.h::page_table_check_alloc.alt_1","include/linux/pageblock-flags.h::pageblock_bits","include/linux/pageblock-flags.h::NR_PAGEBLOCK_BITS","include/linux/pageblock-flags.h::PAGEBLOCK_MIGRATETYPE_MASK"],"text":"Wrappers idle unless global branch selects active path. Type uses three bits with separate skip and isolation bits; exposed bit count rounds to power of two."}],"locks":[{"sids":["include/linux/mmzone.h::pglist_data"],"text":"Node size lock stabilizes start, present, spanned, zone count and deferred cursor under hotplug/deferred init, ordered above zone lock and span seqlock."},{"sids":["include/linux/page_ref.h::page_ref_count","include/linux/page_ref.h::init_page_count","include/linux/page_ref.h::page_ref_add","include/linux/page_ref.h::page_ref_sub","include/linux/page_ref.h::page_ref_freeze","include/linux/page_ref.h::page_ref_unfreeze","include/linux/page_ref.h::page_ref_tracepoint_active.alt_1","include/linux/page_ref.h::page_ref_tracepoint_active.alt_2","include/linux/page_idle.h::folio_test_young","include/linux/page_idle.h::folio_set_young","include/linux/page_idle.h::folio_test_clear_young","include/linux/page_idle.h::folio_test_idle","include/linux/page_idle.h::folio_set_idle","include/linux/page_idle.h::folio_clear_idle"],"text":"Counts use atomics with release on unfreeze and conditional trace; flag accesses hold a metadata reference across the bit operation."}],"pass":1,"phase_map":[{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p14","crown":"A","phase":"F0"},{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p04","crown":"A","phase":"F1"},{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p05","crown":"A","phase":"F3"}],"schema":"lx.dossier.v1","state_machines":[{"sids":["include/linux/page_ext.h::page_ext_init_flatmem_late.alt_1","include/linux/page_ext.h::page_ext_init.alt_1","include/linux/page_ext.h::page_ext_iter_begin","include/linux/page_ext.h::page_ext_iter_next","include/linux/page_ext.h::page_ext_iter_get","include/linux/page_ext.h::for_each_page_ext"],"text":"Iteration rejects empty ranges, starts at zero index, stops on missing record or count reached, advancing by stride or fresh lookup across granularity."},{"sids":["include/linux/page_ref.h::init_page_count","include/linux/page_ref.h::page_ref_add","include/linux/page_ref.h::page_ref_sub","include/linux/page_ref.h::page_ref_add_unless_zero","include/linux/page_ref.h::page_ref_freeze","include/linux/page_ref.h::page_ref_unfreeze","include/linux/page_idle.h::folio_test_young","include/linux/page_idle.h::folio_set_young","include/linux/page_idle.h::folio_test_clear_young","include/linux/page_idle.h::folio_test_idle","include/linux/page_idle.h::folio_set_idle","include/linux/page_idle.h::folio_clear_idle"],"text":"Counts start at one, step arbitrarily, fail conditional increment at zero, freeze expected to zero, and unfreeze zero to nonzero. Youth and idle are independent binary cells."}],"structs":[{"sids":["include/linux/mmzone.h::pglist_data","include/linux/mmzone.h::pg_data_t","include/linux/nodemask_types.h::MAX_NUMNODES","include/linux/nodemask_types.h::__LINUX_NODEMASK_TYPES_H","include/linux/nodemask.h::NODE_MASK_NONE","include/linux/nodemask.h::node_states","include/linux/nodemask.h::nodemask_scratch"],"text":"Node descriptor holds zones, zonelists, counts, map, ranges, waits, daemon state, reserves, cursors, reclaim vector and stats. Masks are fixed bit containers; states cover possible, online, memory, CPU and initiator; scratch holds two masks."},{"sids":["include/linux/mmzone.h::mem_section","include/linux/mmzone.h::mem_section_usage","include/linux/mmzone.h::SUBSECTION_ALIGN_UP","include/linux/mmzone.h::SUBSECTION_ALIGN_DOWN","include/linux/mmzone.h::section_to_usemap","include/linux/mmzone.h::anon_5","include/linux/mmzone.h::SECTION_MARKED_PRESENT","include/linux/mmzone.h::SECTION_HAS_MEM_MAP","include/linux/mmzone.h::SECTION_IS_ONLINE","include/linux/mmzone.h::SECTION_IS_EARLY","include/linux/mmzone.h::SECTION_TAINT_ZONE_DEVICE","include/linux/mmzone.h::SECTION_IS_VMEMMAP_PREINIT","include/linux/mmzone.h::SECTION_MAP_MASK","include/linux/mmzone.h::SECTION_NID_SHIFT"],"text":"Usage pairs callback head with bitmap and flag array as usemap. Descriptors hold encoded map word, usage pointer and extension state as power-of-two. Low bits encode present, mapped, online, early, device and preinit with masks and node shift."},{"sids":["include/linux/page_counter.h::_LINUX_PAGE_COUNTER_H","include/linux/page_counter.h::page_counter","include/linux/oom.h::__INCLUDE_LINUX_OOM_H","include/linux/oom.h::oom_constraint","include/linux/oom.h::oom_control","include/linux/numa_memblks.h::__NUMA_MEMBLKS_H","include/linux/numa_memblks.h::NR_NODE_MEMBLKS","include/linux/numa_memblks.h::numa_memblk"],"text":"Counters track usage, failures, protections, limits, watermarks, flags and parent. OOM control holds lists, masks, order, totals, victim and constraint. NUMA table holds address blocks with owning nodes."},{"sids":["include/linux/page_ext.h::__LINUX_PAGE_EXT_H","include/linux/page_ext.h::page_ext_operations","include/linux/page_ext.h::page_ext_flags","include/linux/page_ext.h::page_ext","include/linux/page_ext.h::page_ext_data","include/linux/page_reporting.h::page_reporting_dev_info","include/linux/page_reporting.h::PAGE_REPORTING_CAPACITY","include/linux/page_frag_cache.h::PAGE_FRAG_CACHE_PFMEMALLOC_BIT","include/linux/page_frag_cache.h::page_frag_cache_init"],"text":"Extension ops hold offset, size and callbacks with flags and iterators. Reporting holds callback, work, state, order and batch limit with zero meaning default. Cache holds one encoded word, zero empty."},{"sids":["include/linux/nodemask_types.h::MAX_NUMNODES","include/linux/nodemask_types.h::NODES_SHIFT.alt_1","include/linux/nodemask_types.h::NODES_SHIFT.alt_2","include/linux/numa.h::NUMA_NO_MEMBLK","include/linux/numa_memblks.h::NR_NODE_MEMBLKS","include/linux/page_counter.h::PAGE_COUNTER_MAX.alt_1","include/linux/page_counter.h::PAGE_COUNTER_MAX.alt_2","include/linux/nodemask.h::node_states"],"text":"Maximum nodes is one shifted by a config shift zeroed when single-node; absent sentinels are negative one; block capacity doubles maximum; counter maximum is a large page-scaled limit."},{"sids":["include/linux/pageblock-flags.h::pageblock_order.alt_1","include/linux/pageblock-flags.h::pageblock_order.alt_2","include/linux/pageblock-flags.h::pageblock_order.alt_3","include/linux/pageblock-flags.h::pageblock_nr_pages","include/linux/pageblock-flags.h::pageblock_align","include/linux/pageblock-flags.h::pageblock_aligned","include/linux/pageblock-flags.h::pageblock_start_pfn","include/linux/pageblock-flags.h::pageblock_end_pfn","include/linux/pageblock-flags.h::PAGEBLOCK_MIGRATETYPE_MASK","include/linux/pageblock-flags.h::PAGEBLOCK_ISO_MASK.alt_1","include/linux/pageblock-flags.h::PAGEBLOCK_ISO_MASK.alt_2"],"text":"Block size is two to a configurable order with align, test and start/end helpers. Migratetype combines three bits; isolation is a dedicated bit in one build and zero in the other."}],"stubs":[{"sid":"include/linux/jump_label.h::static_branch_likely.alt_1","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D13"},{"sid":"include/linux/jump_label.h::static_branch_likely.alt_2","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D13"},{"sid":"include/linux/jump_label.h::static_branch_unlikely.alt_1","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D13"},{"sid":"include/linux/jump_label.h::static_branch_unlikely.alt_2","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D13"},{"sid":"include/asm-generic/bitops/instrumented-atomic.h::set_bit","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D14"},{"sid":"include/linux/bitops.h::test_bit","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D14"},{"sid":"include/asm-generic/bitops/instrumented-atomic.h::clear_bit","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D14"},{"sid":"include/asm-generic/bitops/instrumented-atomic.h::test_and_clear_bit","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D14"},{"sid":"include/asm-generic/bug.h::WARN_ON_ONCE.alt_1","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D17"},{"sid":"include/asm-generic/bug.h::WARN_ON_ONCE.alt_2","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D17"},{"sid":"include/asm-generic/bug.h::WARN_ON_ONCE.alt_3","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D17"},{"sid":"include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_add","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D03"},{"sid":"include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_add_unless","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D03"},{"sid":"include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_cmpxchg","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D03"},{"sid":"include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_dec","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D03"},{"sid":"include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_dec_and_test","state":"stub","target_